  "id": "t13-no-grandchildren-ten-tools-literal",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 4 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 4/L4): a child dispatching any of ten privileged tool names (the four orchestration verbs plus six more from the T13 baseline's own s06-privilege suite: memory, session_search, cronjob, list_models, run_workflow, skill_manage) gets the exact literal \"the '<name>' tool is not available to subagents\" for every single one, on both sides, byte-identical \u2014 no grandchildren, structurally: the child cannot spawn its own child (spawn_session/steer_session/collect_session/delegate_task included). This is oracle-authored text (the exact repr()-quoted name in the message), and it costs zero extra upstream calls beyond the child's own ten decision turns, since every one of these is refused before base dispatch is ever reached.",
